From 5a295e22065bac3a170e9947d21aad96a45e5c03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:26:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add the draws the Hypothesis frontend needs

Three additions to libhegel's generate vocabulary, found by driving it as
a Hypothesis backend:

- hegel_generate_integer_weighted: an integer in [min, max] where given
  keys are drawn with given probabilities and the remaining mass falls to
  the ordinary shaped draw. One plain integer choice, so replay and
  shrinking never consult the weights (HypothesisProvider's `weights`).
- allow_nan alongside finite float bounds: NaN is outside every range, so
  a bounded draw that allows it produces NaN with the usual probability and
  in-range values otherwise, instead of a usage error.
- hegel_string_generator_text_ranges: a text alphabet given as explicit,
  sorted, disjoint codepoint ranges (a frontend's own interval set), with
  surrogates removed as for the existing text generator.

The C header and the frontend's FFI list are regenerated, and the C ABI
tests cover the three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
